{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789852090,"nonce":"BrGEZOk0lOaNlxPiSstV9NaHl0A=","title":"The LLVM headroom gate counts frees and cold calls, keeping nbody's advance on the baseline","message":"llvm_list_entry_has_headroom refuses the LLVM tier to a list-entry body with more than 64 calls, on the ground that calls across the LLVM/Cranelift boundary stay indirect and leave little to optimise. It counts every Call: nbody's advance has 72 after optimisation, of which 46 are intrinsic.free, 21 are the fatal paths of bounds checks and 4 cross the boundary. The trace says \"LLVM promotion skipped for advance: call-heavy list entry\" at every promotion request and the kernel runs on Cranelift for good, 1.05x behind PyPy (NUC, 50 iterations, mean 6.54 vs 6.25 ms).\n\nIntrinsics lower in place and a cold callee is off the hot path; neither is a boundary call. Counting only the rest lets advance through: mean 5.24 ms, ahead of PyPy by 1.16x.","files":null}]}